# Original origin feats for regions and walks of life.
# Format: (name, type, prerequisite, text)
FEATS = [
("Sea Legs", "Origin", None,
 "You gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed, and you can hold your breath for 10 minutes. You have Advantage on saving throws to avoid the Prone condition while you are on a boat or ship, and you can predict the weather at sea for the next 24 hours with one minute of study."),
("Desert Walker", "Origin", None,
 "You need only half the water that other creatures need, and you are naturally adapted to hot climates. Sand, dust, and glare don't make an area Lightly Obscured for you. You gain proficiency in Survival or, if you already have it, Expertise in it."),
("Courtly Poise", "Origin", None,
 "You gain proficiency in Deception or Persuasion. Creatures have Disadvantage on Wisdom (Insight) checks to read your intentions or your mood. When you roll Initiative in a social setting, such as a feast, a trial, or an audience, you can add your Proficiency Bonus to the roll."),
("Streetwise", "Origin", None,
 "You gain proficiency in Deception or Stealth. In a town or city, you can spend 1 hour to learn the local rumors, find a fence or a smuggler, or learn who holds power in a neighborhood. You have Advantage on checks to notice that you are being followed in a settlement."),
("Steadfast Faith", "Origin", None,
 "When you fail a saving throw, you can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to the save, possibly turning it into a success. You can use this benefit a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. You also gain proficiency in Religion."),
("Born Rider", "Origin", None,
 "Mounting or dismounting costs you only 5 feet of movement. You have Advantage on saving throws to avoid falling off a mount. While you ride, your mount's Speed increases by 10 feet, and you can take the Dash or Disengage action for your mount as a Bonus Action. You also gain proficiency in Animal Handling."),
("Crag Walker", "Origin", None,
 "You gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. Difficult Terrain made of rubble, scree, ice, or steep slopes doesn't cost you extra movement. You have Advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks to climb in wind, rain, or ice."),
("Cave Eyes", "Origin", None,
 "You gain Darkvision with a range of 60 feet. If you already have Darkvision, its range increases by 30 feet. You also have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight while you are in Dim Light."),
]
